# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "The gradient floor: a sigil surfaces as itself and stops at its closer"

# The floor stands independent of any vocabulary. A sigil the base reads as a call and a sigil a
# dialect names for itself must BOTH leave the sentence after their closer standing alone.
#
# The floor reaches as far as one line of lookahead reaches, and no further. TiddlyWiki builds a
# call wherever `>>` stands ahead ANYWHERE in the source — the same line or twenty below — and
# builds nothing at all where none does. A TextMate pattern sees one line, so it cannot tell those
# two apart, and a blank-line bound that answered the second broke the first: measured over 700
# carriers and 16087 openers, 116 close on a later line and NONE lack a closer entirely. So the
# region runs to its closer, and `corpus/carrier-ledger.txt` rules the case that has no closer.

<<~ ahu #broken

  >>
#  ^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext meta.variable.call.block.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.call.block.end.tiddlywiki5

SENTINEL reads as an ordinary paragraph.
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

<<^ code="&#x0001;" ? -> lar:///the.frame.opens

>>
#^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext meta.variable.call.block.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.call.block.end.tiddlywiki5

SENTINEL reads as an ordinary paragraph.
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
